                    {
                        "sense_id": "2e35c7e5-821d-33d1-af27-350db191eb5e",
                        "entry_id": "d36338d0-e447-375c-afc6-07611e038a69",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A company operating in only one industry or line of business; often specifically a bank specializing in credit card issuance."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "093823a9-1eb5-48c0-b4d8-b83d993921a3",
                                "sense_id": "2e35c7e5-821d-33d1-af27-350db191eb5e",
                                "text": "The other leading monolines in 2002 were Capital One and Providian."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "c204792f-b724-37de-9450-cae7e897c65e",
                        "entry_id": "d36338d0-e447-375c-afc6-07611e038a69",
                        "glosses": [
                            "An insurer specialized in insuring investment-grade securities against loss."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "2a832a39-e5b0-4e72-82ea-100026b1e41a",
                                "sense_id": "c204792f-b724-37de-9450-cae7e897c65e",
                                "text": "The premium charged by the monoline is not for funding expected losses, as with insurance, but for enhancing an investment-grade security to a AAA level."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "1a01b9db-1c5f-3dfa-b03c-0ab016b6032d",
                        "entry_id": "d36338d0-e447-375c-afc6-07611e038a69",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A font line of consistent width, as occurs when imitating pencil script."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "146f512b-2bbe-4831-9932-58aa0cc040fe",
                                "sense_id": "1a01b9db-1c5f-3dfa-b03c-0ab016b6032d",
                                "text": "[…] monolines appear everywhere in the art of the Western letter, and have shaped the alphabet's development as much as the edged line of the broad pen."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "1db3c13e-6929-3501-80d6-4a0db752109a",
                        "entry_id": "d36338d0-e447-375c-afc6-07611e038a69",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A length of monofilament line, used for culturing forms of seaweed."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "57b9d471-cadb-466d-a56f-f1d4a040c989",
                                "sense_id": "1db3c13e-6929-3501-80d6-4a0db752109a",
                                "text": "A module consists of 21 monolines; a monoline on the other hand is 20 feet (6 m) long and consists of a nylon line plus 3 stakes— 2 at both ends and one at the middle— and 30 plants."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "3579c6c6-8905-311c-9c53-adca8306d06c",
                        "entry_id": "d36338d0-e447-375c-afc6-07611e038a69",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A type of composing machine in which each line of type is cast as a single slug."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "dated"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "16c184cf-aa1d-4fa6-810d-67d79eb54921",
                                "sense_id": "3579c6c6-8905-311c-9c53-adca8306d06c",
                                "text": "With the straight matter being set on the linotype or monoline, the hand compositor was left with what he claimed was the most 'skilled' part of his old work."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "1fe79c52-7ed9-3f0d-ae19-46eb0276b28b",
                        "entry_id": "d36338d0-e447-375c-afc6-07611e038a69",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A single spectrum line."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "8c6588c7-4d39-4d71-a128-3d15b5acc154",
                                "sense_id": "1fe79c52-7ed9-3f0d-ae19-46eb0276b28b",
                                "text": "The spectrum of the MS sample also includes the central broad singlet of the nitrous austenite, which is simulated as the superposition of a monoline and a doublet."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
